faq:
  - q: What is a true rate per mile?
    a: It is the load pay divided by all the miles the truck has to run for that trip, including empty miles to the pickup or between stops. The loaded rate ignores those empty miles.
  - q: Should I include the fuel surcharge in the pay?
    a: Use the same money you will actually invoice or collect for the trip. If the confirmation shows a linehaul plus a fuel surcharge, adding both is usually the honest comparison. If you only want a linehaul rate, leave the surcharge out and be consistent from load to load.
  - q: Are the starting numbers average rates?
    a: No. They are example figures so the calculator has something to show when the page opens. They are not a market average, a DAT or Truckstop rate, or a recommendation.
  - q: Does this tell me whether a load is profitable?
    a: No. Profit also depends on fuel, tolls, maintenance, the driver’s hours, and your cost per mile. This page only compares pay with miles.
